I do not understand what you are trying to say; I was saying I would
like to see smooth characters on my display as I play nethack.  I think
you were trying to suggest that using high resolution fonts is wasteful
in some information theoretic way.

But... 8x14 is a normal sort of font to render fixed width text in.
Each character then is 108 bits or so.  But... English has only perhaps
3 or 4 bits of information per character (c.f. Shannon).  So, if
redundancy is the concern, I think we're in trouble if our goal is to
maximise our information efficiency of even a standard 80x25 VGA
display; we're already one and a half order to two of magnitude wasting
the capacity when we play nethack.

On the other hand, if, like me, you'd like an _even more redundant
font_ in order to get very, very smooth "o" characters, then, hey,
great news: a large, well designed font can help here.

